## Answers to Your Questions

### 1. What methods does `TBClient` expose?

`TBClient` is an instance of the `Client` interface from the `tigerbeetle-node` package (v0.17.5). It exposes these methods:

| Method | Signature | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `createAccounts` | `(batch: Account[]) => Promise<CreateAccountResult[]>` | Create one or more accounts |
| `createTransfers` | `(batch: Transfer[]) => Promise<CreateTransferResult[]>` | Create one or more transfers |
| `lookupAccounts` | `(batch: AccountID[]) => Promise<Account[]>` | Look up accounts by their IDs |
| `lookupTransfers` | `(batch: TransferID[]) => Promise<Transfer[]>` | Look up transfers by their IDs |
| `getAccountTransfers` | `(filter: AccountFilter) => Promise<Transfer[]>` | Get all transfers for a given account |
| `getAccountBalances` | `(filter: AccountFilter) => Promise<AccountBalance[]>` | Get historical account balances |
| `queryAccounts` | `(filter: QueryFilter) => Promise<Account[]>` | Query accounts by user_data, ledger, code, etc. |
| `queryTransfers` | `(filter: QueryFilter) => Promise<Transfer[]>` | Query transfers by user_data, ledger, code, etc. |
| `destroy` | `() => void` | Close the client connection |

The higher-level `ITigerBeetle` interface in this project wraps the raw client into convenience methods: `createAccount`, `getAccount`, `transferFunds`, `getTransaction`, `createTransfer`.

### 2. What types does `TB` provide?

`TB` is a namespace re-export of everything from `tigerbeetle-node`. The most important types are:

**Account** (the core data type):
```ts
type Account = {
  id: bigint;               // Account identifier (use TB.id() to generate)
  debits_pending: bigint;   // Amount of pending debits
  debits_posted: bigint;    // Amount of posted (settled) debits
  credits_pending: bigint;  // Amount of pending credits
  credits_posted: bigint;   // Amount of posted (settled) credits
  user_data_128: bigint;    // Custom user data (128-bit) — used here for userId
  user_data_64: bigint;     // Custom user data (64-bit)
  user_data_32: number;     // Custom user data (32-bit)
  reserved: number;         // Reserved field
  ledger: number;           // Ledger identifier (e.g., 85 = WALLET_LEDGER_CODE)
  code: number;             // Currency code (e.g., 356 = INR, 840 = USD)
  flags: number;            // Bitfield of AccountFlags
  timestamp: bigint;        // nanoseconds since TigerBeetle epoch
};
```

**Transfer**:
```ts
type Transfer = {
  id: bigint;
  debit_account_id: bigint;     // Source account
  credit_account_id: bigint;    // Destination account
  amount: bigint;
  pending_id: bigint;
  user_data_128: bigint;
  user_data_64: bigint;
  user_data_32: number;
  timeout: number;
  ledger: number;
  code: number;
  flags: number;                // Bitfield of TransferFlags
  timestamp: bigint;
};
```

**Enums / Types re-exported as `TB.*`**:
| Export | Kind | Notable values |
